methods.doc:
applyImpulse changes the body's velocity at once by an impulse {x, y}
(mass times velocity), waking it. Fails with StateError when the body or
its world has been destroyed.

functions.doc:
create makes a cache holding capacity entries that live ttl seconds;
invalid values fall back to 100 entries and 300 seconds.

Deprecated: use cache.new({capacity: capacity, ttl: milliseconds}) instead.

methods.doc:
get returns the value stored under key and marks it most recently used, or
null when key is missing or has expired. A stored null also reads as null;
use has to tell them apart.

columns returns the column names of table in table order, or an empty
array when there is no such table. Throws ValueError for an invalid name;
fails like db.exec.

setTo replaces the To addresses with addresses, an array of strings;
addresses already on the message are skipped. Fails with ValueError,
changing nothing, when any address is invalid.

functions.doc:
has reports whether data carries EXIF metadata: a JPEG, PNG or WebP image
with an EXIF block, a TIFF image, or a raw EXIF block. It never fails;
corrupt or unrecognised data gives false.

packages.about:
option, some() and none() are built into the compiler. Use an option when
null is a value worth keeping, so "absent" and "present but null" differ;
most optional values are plain nullable types (T?).

methods.doc:
setFontSize sets the font size in points for text written from now on;
on a page with nothing on it yet, flowing text starts one line of the new
size below the top margin. Throws ValueError for a size that isn't more than 0 and at most 1000.

functions.doc:
waitPID waits for a child process by ID and returns {success, pid, code}
or {success, error}.

Deprecated: use process.start(command, args) and Child.wait() instead.

methods.doc:
signal sends a signal to the process: "INT", "TERM", "KILL", "HUP" or
"QUIT" (a "SIG" prefix is allowed). Throws ValueError for any other name;
fails with StateError when the process has already exited.

packages.about:
This is the one source of randomness: random.seed(n) makes every random
function repeat the same sequence. random.int(1, 6) includes both ends;
random.number() is from 0 up to 1, as JavaScript's Math.random() is.

methods.doc:
box returns where the ray first meets a box around a center {x, y, z}
with a size {x, y, z}: {hit, distance, point, normal}, where distance,
point and normal are null when hit is false.

bindJSON decodes the JSON request body into out, an object (whose keys
are set from the body) or a class instance. Fails with ParseError when the body isn't valid JSON for out;
left uncaught, that answers the client 400.

close stops every download, disconnects from all peers and stops
listening. Downloaded files stay on disk. Closing twice is a no-op;
using the client or its downloads afterwards throws StateError.

functions.doc:
font names the font in the TrueType or OpenType file at path, for a
theme's font or a tag's font prop. Pages serve the file to the browser;
windows draw with it.

toJSON converts YAML text to JSON text, or a JSON {"error": message}
object when the YAML is malformed.

Deprecated: use json.stringify(yaml.parse(text)) instead.
